			"notes": "Bugfix release for the registry-driven pickers in 1.11.0.\n\n- Fixed the trim-material icon strip being empty and unclickable on 1.21.11 and 26.2 (registry keys came out as garbage ids).\n- Fixed enchantment and attribute ids getting the same garbage (levels and commands are correct now).\n- Attributes and all picker ids now keep their namespace, so modded enchantments, attributes, items, mobs, potions, effects and trims actually work when picked (before, anything not in the minecraft namespace lost it).\n- Attribute fields accept vanilla (max_health), namespaced (minecraft:max_health) and modded (yourmod:reinforce) ids; legacy generic./player. prefixes still work.\n- Removed the last dead option lists; 25-check regression suite runs on every build.\n\nPick the jar for your Minecraft version. 26.x needs Java 25; 1.21.x needs Java 21."
		},
